      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $A$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 3 is $-5\\ne 0$, above the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is diagonal: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 3 is $-5\\ne 0$, off the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "77b18910-77d2-5635-a071-c32ceb58dcb3",
